<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean-Baptiste Jourdan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1762–1833</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean-Baptiste Jourdan was a French general and Marshal of the Empire. He won the Battle of Fleurus in 1794, securing the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> for the French Republic, and gave his name to the Jourdan Law of 1798 that introduced conscription. He governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1801–1802 and later served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-bonaparte">Joseph Bonaparte</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, where he was defeated at Vitoria in 1813.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-jourdan.jpg" alt="Jean-Baptiste Jourdan" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Joseph-Marie Vien · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_mar%C3%A9chal_Jourdan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
